<h1 id="ruskey">Ruskey 🦀</h1>
<p>An implementation of the Monkey programming language interpreter in Rust, based on the book “Writing An Interpreter In Go” by Thorsten Ball.</p>
<h2 id="about">About</h2>
<p><strong>🚧 Work In Progress 🚧</strong></p>
<p>This project is currently under active development. It’s a Rust implementation of the Monkey programming language introduced in the book “Writing An Interpreter In Go”. It serves as both a learning exercise for Rust and interpreter design.</p>
<p>The Monkey language features:</p>
<ul>
<li>C-like syntax</li>
<li>Variable bindings</li>
<li>Integer and boolean data types</li>
<li>Functions as first-class citizens</li>
<li>Closures</li>
<li>A simple object system</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="project-structure">Project Structure</h2>
<pre><code>ruskey/
├── src/           # Source code
│   ├── token.rs   # Token definitions
│   ├── lexer.rs   # Lexical analyzer
│   ├── ast.rs     # Abstract Syntax Tree
│   ├── parser.rs  # Parser
│   └── ...
├── tests/         # Test suite
└── ...
</code></pre>
<h2 id="progress">Progress</h2>
